  "configuration_id": "config_006",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_005 (rna_only, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool) achieved the best accuracy so far at 0.650, a large jump over its singleprofile counterpart (config_004, 0.520). This confirms multiprofile is highly beneficial. Uncertainty: whether the gain is primarily from having multiple profiles or from the specific avgpool aggregation, and whether a more expressive transformer aggregation could further exploit the multiprofile structure. This experiment (config_006) isolates the aggregation variable by swapping avgpool → transformer while holding encoder (scvi_n200) and profile setting (multiprofile) constant. It is the best next step because it directly extends the current best configuration with a single controlled change, giving a clean read on whether more sophisticated profile aggregation can push accuracy beyond 0.650 before we invest remaining budget in multimodal fusion or alternative encoders."
}

